      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "After further testing in Video Player Showroom (https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_985acb34-cc17-4b5a-85ae-04ade5195059), it appears that the Unity default video player works fine (running a HEAD request on normal, when I test with my own server), but the AVPro-based one crashes VRChat. Interesting. This occurs with the 1080p 60 fps version of Big Buck Bunny, bbb_sunflower_1080p_60fps_normal.mp4, hosted on my own server so that I can log requests. I am guessing the --enable-avpro-in-proton command is a Unity option specific to the Unity video player, but this does not explain why it crashes now when it never did before. Maybe it is because it is partly working now, but not enough to not be buggy?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
