      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{605411844c33c840d57e2f1d|full_name}: Unity asset bundles are compiled differently for Linux and Windows. Implementing a system to convert this stuff at runtime in the game is nonsensical. VRChat has been pretty supportive of Proton, and some members of the dev team use Linux on the daily and understand this too.\nI wrote further on this in other replies on this post, please feel free to check those out. I will say, Proton video support is actively being worked on. But work from the AVPro team will have to be done as well for streams to function properly.\nTL;DR Proton > Native in this case.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
